## GENERAL:

1. THE MAKE-UP AIR UNIT SHALL BE CONTROLLED BY A DEDICATED CONTROLLER AND NETWORKED TO THE BAS. CONTROL PANEL SHALL BE HOUSED IN THE MAU SERVICE VESTIBULE.
2. ALL PROGRAMMING SHALL RESIDE LOCAL TO THE CONTROLLER AND UNIT SHALL CONTINUE TO OPERATE UPON A LOSS OF NETWORK COMMUNICATIONS.
3. THE STEAM GENERATOR SHALL BE CONTROLLED BY THE MANUFACTURER'S INTEGRAL MICROPROCESSOR CONTROLLER AND INTERFACED TO THE BAS VIA BACNET IP.
4. ALL SETPOINTS SHALL BE ADJUSTABLE.
5. REFER TO THE ROOM CRITERIA SHEET FOR SPACE TEMPERATURE, SPACE HUMIDITY, AND SPACE DIFFERENTIAL PRESSURE SETPOINTS.

---

## LEAD / STANDBY OPERATION:

1. THE MAKE-UP AIR SYSTEM SHALL OPERATE AT ALL TIMES, UNLESS OFF DUE TO SAFETY OR MANUAL DISCONNECT.
2. THE MAKE-UP AIR SYSTEM CONSISTS OF PARALLEL AIR HANDLERS IN AN N+1, LEAD / STANDBY CONFIGURATION. ONE AIR HANDLER SHALL OPERATE AT A TIME.
3. THE LEAD UNIT ASSIGNMENT SHALL BE ROTATED WEEKLY.
4. UPON FAILURE OF THE LEAD AIR HANDLER, THE STANDBY AIR HANDLER SHALL AUTOMATICALLY START AND AN ALARM SHALL BE INDICATED.
5. BEFORE THE STANDBY UNIT IS ALLOWED TO START, THE CHW AND HW PREHEAT VALVES ON THE STANDBY UNIT SHALL BE STROKED FULLY OPEN TO PURGE AND PRIME THE COILS FOR 2 MINUTES PRIOR TO STARTING THE STANDBY UNIT. ONCE THE UNIT IS STARTED, THE VALVE OPERATION SHALL REVERT BACK TO NORMAL CONTROL.

---

## FAN AND DAMPER CONTROL:

1. WHEN A UNIT IS CALLED TO OPERATE, THE OUTDOOR AIR DAMPER AND SUPPLY AIR DAMPER SHALL OPEN AND BE PROVEN OPEN VIA AN END SWITCH.
2. EACH AIR HANDLER CONSISTS OF AN N-1 FAN ARRAY. DURING NORMAL OPERATION, ALL FANS SHALL RUN AT ALL TIMES.
3. THE FAN SPEED SHALL MODULATE TO MAINTAIN THE DUCT DIFFERENTIAL PRESSURE SETPOINT.
4. UPON FAILURE OF ANY FAN (BASED ON THE VFD STATUS OR CT), THE REMAINING FAN SHALL INCREASE IN SPEED TO MAINTAIN THE DUCT DIFFERENTIAL PRESSURE SETPOINT, AND AN ALARM SHALL BE INDICATED.

---

## HEATING MODE:

1. THE HOT WATER PREHEAT COIL SHALL MAINTAIN A LAT OF 45 DEG F AT ALL TIMES.
2. DURING HEATING MODE, THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT SHALL BE RESET LINEARLY BASED ON THE POSITION OF THE WORST CASE SENSIBLE COOLING COIL CONTROL VALVES IN EACH OF ASSOCIATED SPACES.
   A. WHEN ALL SENSIBLE COOLING COIL VALVES ARE FULLY CLOSED, THE SUPPLY AIR SETPOINT SHALL BE 60 DEG F.
   B. WHEN ANY SENSIBLE COOLING COIL VALVE IS FULLY OPENED, THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT SHALL BE 45 DEG F.
   C. THE LINEAR RESET IN BETWEEN SHALL BE BASED ON THE WORST CASE VALVE.
3. THE FIRST MEANS OF HEATING SHALL BE BY THE HOT WATER PRE-HEAT COIL. THE CONTROL VALVE SHALL MODULATE TO MAINTAIN THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT.
4. IF THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT CANNOT BE MAINTAINED BY THE PRE-HEAT COIL ALONE, THE HOT WATER RE-HEAT COIL CONTROL VALVE SHALL MODULATE OPEN TO MAINTAIN THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT.

---

## HUMIDIFICATION MODE:

1. THE STEAM GENERATOR AND DISPERSION GRID SYSTEM SHALL BE ENABLED UPON A DROP IN OUTSIDE AIR DEWPOINT BELOW 46 DEG F OR ANY ROOM RH IS BELOW 40% FOR MORE THAN 5 MINUTES.
2. THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT SHALL BE RESET TO 60 DEG F.
3. FLOW SHALL BE PROVEN VIA THE AIRFLOW SWITCH.
4. THE HUMIDIFIER SHALL MAINTAIN THE SPACE RELATIVE HUMIDITY SETPOINT FOR THE WORST CASE SPACE.
5. THE STEAM GENERATOR SYSTEM SHALL BE PLACED IN STANDBY FOR 24 HRS UPON A RISE IN OUTSIDE AIR DEWPOINT ABOVE 48 DEG F FOR MORE THAN 5 MINUTES.

---

## COOLING MODE:

1. COOLING MODE SHALL BE ENABLED WHEN OUTSIDE AIR TEMPERATURE RISES ABOVE 50 DEG F, AND OUTSIDE AIR DEWPOINT IS BELOW 47 DEG F FOR MORE THAN 5 MINUTES.
2. THE COOLING COIL CONTROL VALVE SHALL MODULATE TO MAINTAIN THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT OF 47.5 DEG F.
3. COOLING MODE SHALL BE DISABLED WHEN OUTSIDE AIR TEMPERATURE DROPS BELOW 48 DEG F FOR MORE THAN 5 MINUTES.

---

## DEHUMIDIFICATION MODE:

1. DEHUMIDIFICATION MODE SHALL BE ENABLED UPON A RISE IN OUTSIDE AIR DEWPOINT ABOVE 47 DEG F FOR MORE THAN 5 MINUTES, OR A RISE IN SPACE RH OF MORE THAN 2% FOR MORE THAN 1 MINUTE.
2. THE COOLING COIL CONTROL VALVE SHALL MODULATE TO MAINTAIN A CC LEAVING AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT OF 47.5 DEG F.
3. THE RE-HEAT COIL CONTROL VALVE SHALL MODULATE TO MAINTAIN THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT.
4. THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT SHALL BE RESET LINEARLY BASED ON THE POSITION OF THE WORST CASE SENSIBLE COOLING COIL CONTROL VALVES IN EACH OF THE ASSOCIATED SPACES.
   A. WHEN ALL SENSIBLE COOLING COIL VALVES ARE FULLY CLOSED, THE SUPPLY AIR SETPOINT SHALL BE 60 DEG F.
   B. WHEN ANY SENSIBLE COOLING COIL VALVE IS FULLY OPENED, THE SUPPLY AIR TEMPERATURE SETPOINT SHALL BE 45 DEG F.
   C. THE LINEAR RESET IN BETWEEN SHALL BE BASED ON THE WORST CASE VALVE.

---

## MAINTENANCE MODE:

1. PROVIDE A MAINTENANCE OVERRIDE SWITCH IN THE FRONT END GRAPHICS FOR EACH TUNNEL OF THE AIR HANDLER.
2. ACTIVATION OF THE MAINTENANCE MODE SHALL CAUSE THE SELECTED UNIT TO SHUT DOWN AND THE STANDBY UNIT TO START VIA THE NORMAL CHANGEOVER SEQUENCE.
3. NO ALARMS SHALL BE GENERATED FOR A UNIT WHILE IN THIS MODE.
4. MAINTENANCE MODE SHALL PERSIST UNTIL THE OPERATOR MANUALLY CANCELS IT.
5. A UNIT IN MAINTENANCE MODE FOR LONGER THAN 24 HRS SHALL GENERATE AN ALARM IN THE BAS.

